00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: God gives the jinns a longer life, and more ability to fly in the universe and study God's signs.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:48.000
But the humans, they are given 7:172.

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: Read it. Read 7:172 again.

00:34:55.000 --> 00:35:03.000
A man: Rashad, jinns have that much ability to go to other universe because they have to be more clear than the people?

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, because they already made up their mind very strongly that Satan is right.

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: You see, here God, God is the children of Adam, not the children of Satan, not the jinns.

00:35:17.000 --> 00:35:23.000
A man: Exactly, (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:30.000
A woman: Difference, difference (unintelligible)

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Not really, no, it's just that, that there's a different allegorical Heaven for them.

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.000
Because...

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.000
How do I...

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Let us say, compare you with a tree.

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
You and a tree.

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:50.000
Think of yourself as two creatures.

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:56.000
And I'm saying, gonna put you and the tree, I'm gonna put you both in Heaven, I'm gonna give you steak,

00:35:56.000 --> 00:36:01.000
I'm gonna give you potatoes, and rice, and fruit.

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:04.000
Do you think the tree will go for that?

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: Do you understand what I said?

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:17.000
A woman: Yes, oh yeah, (unintelligible)

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, you are a creature and the tree is a creature.

00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: And I'm telling you, I'm gonna put you both in Heaven, where you can eat steak every day.

00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:26.000
A woman: Then, no.

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: No what?

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.000
A woman: Because the tree doesn't like the steak. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the humans and the jinns are two different creatures.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:43.000
And God is telling us "I'm going put you in gardens with grapes and pomegranates and fruit."

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:47.000
The jinns don't, the jinns don't care about that.

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, God is telling them that you're gonna have your own Heaven which is with different things.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:55.000
A woman: But actually it's going to be the same.

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, actually it's gonna be the same Heaven.

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:07.000
Are they (unintelligible) souls the same as ours?

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Um-hum. (unintelligible)

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: Mã Shã Allãh. She likes it first.

00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:37.000
A woman: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:40.000
A woman: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: No, it just fixed.

00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: They're creatures.

00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, it's my sleeping time, brothers and sisters, so I'm gonna retire and see you in the morning, IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:49.000
Audience: IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: I got up at what time?

00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:53.000
A man: This morning? Dr. Khalifa: Yes. A man: 4.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.000
A man: (unintelligible) A man: (unintelligible)

00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, it was 1 o'clock.

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:02.000
A woman: Are you working?

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Well, I left home at 1, so I got here about 20 after 1.

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:12.000
This is why people laugh at me when I say it's my sleeping time.

00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's chicken sleeping time.

00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:21.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:23.000
A woman: Sura Tawbah.

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: 50.

00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:41.000
[9:50] If something good happens to you, they hurt, and if an affliction befalls you, they say, "We told you so," as they turn away rejoicing.

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:44.000
These are all descriptions of the hypocrites.

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:45.000
[9:51] Say, "Nothing happens ...

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: ... whether we're submitters or objectors.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:51.000
So God is telling us in 51,

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:55.000
[9:51] Say, "Nothing happens to us, except what GOD has decreed for us. ...

00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:59.000
And we have to accept it or object to it.

00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:05.000
A submitter accepts whatever happens cheerfully.

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:10.000
Underline cheerfully, 19 lines, under cheerfully.

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:18.000
[9:51] ... In GOD the believers shall trust."

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:24.000
In other words, if you're a believer, you must trust that God will take care of you. God guarantees it for you.

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:30.000
And if something appears to be bad, you must know there's some good reason for it.

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:53.000
[9:52] Say, "You can only expect for us one of two good things in war (victory or martyrdom), while we expect for you condemnation from GOD and retribution from Him, or at our hands. Therefore, wait, and we will wait along with you."

00:39:54.000 --> 00:40:01.000
[9:53] Say, "Spend, willingly or unwillingly. Nothing will be accepted from you, for you are evil people."

00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:06.000
Rejectors of God's messenger observed the Salat prayers.

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:23.000
[9:54] What prevented the acceptance of their spending is that they disbelieved in GOD and His messenger, and when they observed the Contact Prayers (Salat),* they observed them lazily, and when they gave to charity, they did so grudgingly.

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:28.000
This is an important verse you should remember, it's 9:54, remember it.

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:32.000
When the people tell you that they think that Salat began with Muhammad.

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:35.000
They think there was no Salat before the prophet Muhammad.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:38.000
You tell them, remind them of this verse.

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:46.000
These are people who rejected the prophet, they disbelieved in God, but they were doing the five Contact Prayers. The word Salat is very specific.

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:49.000
Because Salat existed before the prophet.

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just at the time, they had been, they had been corrupted by idol worship.

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:59.000
A man: You're saying that today (unintelligible)

00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly, exactly, same thing today.

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: 9:54, this is another proof that the Contact Prayers (Salat) existed before the Quran.

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:26.000
Mahmoud: (unintelligible)

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, this is a good point because this, this verse was revealed probably less than a year before the prophet's death,

00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:43.000
and this is my chance to give Parivash a public apology. In Sura... because I misunderstood her question yesterday.

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:53.000
She was saying that the verses at the end of Sura 15 about people who accept the Quran partially, could not possibly be

00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:57.000
applicable to the time of the prophet, because the Quran itself

00:41:57.000 --> 00:42:01.000
was, was being revealed, it was not in existence really.

00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:06.000
Even when the prophet died, they left the Quran in the chronological sequence,

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:14.000
with instructions on the side, it was, it was not organized at all into a Quran. Now, we have the Quran.

00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:22.000
This is the Quran, the format that God wants, and it did not exist until 20 years after the prophet's death,

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:24.000
Dr. Khalifa: they tried to put it together.

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Look at those people, they are not believers, but they are happy and rich, and this and that.

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:34.000
But they are not happy, you have to take that word out.

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:39.000
Because God says He would cause the money and the children to be the source of misery for them.

00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:49.000
Then after all this misery, they leave the world as disbelievers.

00:42:51.000 --> 00:43:00.000
[9:56] They swear by GOD that they belong with you, while they do not belong with you; they are divisive people.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:06.000
They will create division, they will create confusion, because the statements that come out of their mouths is that of disbelief.

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:15.000
[9:57] If they could find any refuge, or caves, or a hiding place, they would go to it, rushing.

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:29.000
[9:58] Some of them criticize your distribution of the charities; if they are given therefrom, they become satisfied, but if they are not given therefrom, they become objectors.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:43.000
[9:59] They should be satisfied with what GOD and His messenger have given them. They should have said, "GOD suffices us. GOD will provide for us from His bounties, through His messenger. We are seeking only GOD."

00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:48.000
And here is the distribution system for charities other than Zakat.

00:43:49.000 --> 00:43:51.000
It also applies to Zakat.

00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:54.000
[9:60] Charities shall go to the poor, ...

00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.000
So in Zakat, it says your parents first.

00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:01.000
They have to be poor.

00:44:02.000 --> 00:44:12.000
If they are, they are not poor, then you go to the next line, which is relatives: cousins, aunts, nephews, nieces, uncles.

00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:38.000
[9:60] Charities shall go to the poor, the needy, the workers who collect them, the new converts, to free the slaves, to those burdened by sudden expenses, in the cause of GOD, and to the traveling alien. Such is GOD's commandment. GOD is Omniscient, Most Wise.

00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:55.000
[9:61] Some of them hurt the prophet by saying, "He is all ears!" Say, "It is better for you that he listens to you. He believes in GOD, and trusts the believers. He is a mercy for those among you who believe." Those who hurt GOD's messenger have incurred a painful retribution.

00:44:56.000 --> 00:45:06.000
[9:62] They swear by GOD to you, to please you, when GOD and His messenger are more worthy of pleasing, if they are really believers.

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:11.000
Retribution for Opposing God and His Messenger

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:21.000
[9:63] Did they not know that anyone who opposes GOD and His messenger has incurred the fire of Hell forever? This is the worst humiliation.

00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:33.000
[9:64] The hypocrites worry that a sura may be revealed exposing what is inside their hearts. Say, "Go ahead and mock. GOD will bring out what you are worried about."

00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:44.000
[9:65] If you ask them, they would say, "We were only joking and playing." Say, "Do you realize that you are mocking GOD, and His revelations, and His messenger?"

00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:55.000
[9:66] Do not apologize. You have disbelieved after having believed. If we pardon some of you, we will punish others among you, as a consequence of their transgressions.

00:45:56.000 --> 00:46:08.000
[9:67] The hypocrite men and the hypocrite women belong with each other—they advocate evil and prohibit righteousness, and they are stingy. They forgot GOD, so He forgot them. The hypocrites are truly wicked.

00:46:09.000 --> 00:46:23.000
[9:68] GOD promises the hypocrite men and the hypocrite women, as well as the disbelievers, the fire of Hell. They abide therein forever. It suffices them. GOD has condemned them; they have incurred an unending retribution.

00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:31.000
So, here we read four pages, most of them about the hypocrites, because they sit, sit with us, and they...

00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:36.000
we look on them as believers, and then they talk to some of us, and people listen to them.

00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:45.000
And what, what comes out will cause doubt in the hearts of, in the hearts of the believers.

00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:49.000
But God reserves the lowest pit of Hell for them, because, because of this.

00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:58.000
Because they look like believers, act like believers, so we have to be, we have to be aware as we grow.

00:46:59.000 --> 00:47:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just because we're all here in the same room doesn't mean... you have to be careful to what you listen. This is a test for all of us.

00:47:08.000 --> 00:47:11.000
A woman: Because they are more dangerous than you think. Dr. Khalifa: Exactly. Yeah.

00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: They could be very, very loving, friendly people, and, you know, they're with us, and...

00:47:20.000 --> 00:47:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: Then, they, they stab you. A woman: Because they...

00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:26.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, in fact, we have, we have many examples of this.

00:47:29.000 --> 00:47:36.000
People that have been with us and very strong, who became very close and very friendly, but now we know they are not believers.

00:47:37.000 --> 00:47:42.000
Well, because things are happening progressively, and there's a drop-out point for some people.

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:49.000
So even though they believed, when the messengership point came, for example, they, they couldn't take it.

00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:52.000
But they continue to come with us and come to the meeting.

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: You know a few of those.

00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Okay, we'll have five minutes of discussion.

00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:10.000
A man: And then charity starts with the immediate relative (unintelligible)

00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no, charity is something that's on the spot.

