Earthquake comes and destroys San Francisco, and the people on the street hungry, and

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: you don't even know their names, you help them.

00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:25.000
A man: That's what is unlimited?

00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right. Because it's limited by your means, and by not being too extravagant. Go ahead.

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:45.000
A woman: (unintelligible) If you have a, a cousin, or something like that's poor and, but very disbelieving, arrogant,

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:54.000
all that, and then there's an orphan, that is, you know, believing, and needs it even more,

00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:57.000
A woman: you still give it to the cousin, (unintelligible)?

00:48:57.000 --> 00:49:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, give the Zakat to the relative first. Unless, unless he's fighting you.

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:09.000
If he's just disbelieving, he hasn't made a decision, he doesn't know, but he's not fighting you actively,

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:12.000
then you have to give the Zakat to the relative first.

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:15.000
For God's sake, yes.

00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:24.000
Because your cousin, who's not fighting you, maybe next week he'll read the Quran, discover God, and become better than you and me, right?

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:28.000
And maybe, when you help him, this will cause him to believe.

00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:32.000
Says "Wow, this is a good system! Those believers are charitable."

00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, God tells us to consider them potential believers.

00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:40.000
A man: Charity begins at home.

00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's it.

00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:53.000
A man: Rashad, the people, like, I think everybody is going to get the message

00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: IN SHAA ALLAH. A man: IN SHAA ALLAH

00:49:55.000 --> 00:50:07.000
